(7687909, 1258979, 4008, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> This is an amazing work - well done. I love the off centered composition as well as the pose, the light and the implementation of the anagram (no harm that you misspelled one word)<br/>Congrats! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, I spent quite some time to get the pose as I wanted, since it needed the express the desperation, it needed to show the mask, and I wanted the arms to pick up the light and show this balanced N shape, even though the  body is almost perpendicular to the camera. I had to open up the left arm to show the mask, I had to push the right shoulder forward, elbows resting on a chair set at an angle, and then I had to put the hands flat on the head (2 seconds after pushing the remote ;-) ). A more natural "desperation" pose produced a much more messy picture that I did not like, with arms on the head, second arm hardly visible and mask hardly visible. It would not get the link with COVID across.</td>', 'Originally posted by primabarbara: This is an amazing work - well done. I love the off centered composition as well as the pose, the light and the implementation of the anagram (no harm that you misspelled one word)Congrats!   Thanks, I spent quite some time to get the pose as I wanted, since it needed the express the desperation, it needed to show the mask, and I wanted the arms to pick up the light and show this balanced N shape, even though the  body is almost perpendicular to the camera. I had to open up the left arm to show the mask, I had to push the right shoulder forward, elbows resting on a chair set at an angle, and then I had to put the hands flat on the head (2 seconds after pushing the remote ;-) ). A more natural "desperation" pose produced a much more messy picture that I did not like, with arms on the head, second arm hardly visible and mask hardly visible. It would not get the link with COVID across.', '2021-02-24 05:00:33.000000', NULL, 0),
